\description{
Models the change of a product response over time. Supported capabilities:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Decay models}: zero-order / first-order kinetics, Weibull decay,
exponential decay to a plateau.
\item \strong{Shelf-life prediction}: based on the ICH Q1E guideline, predicts the
shelf life from the lower confidence bound of the response.
\item \strong{Multi-temperature acceleration}: uses the Arrhenius equation to
extrapolate the time effect at a target (e.g. room) temperature.
}
}
\details{
\strong{Theoretical references}:
\itemize{
\item ICH Q1E (2003). \emph{Evaluation for Stability Data}.
\item Arrhenius, S. (1889). \emph{Uber die Reaktionsgeschwindigkeit bei der Inversion
von Rohrzucker}.
\item Weibull, W. (1951). \emph{A statistical distribution function of wide
applicability}.
}
